  "assessment": "The published argon reproduction is robust to a factor-two timestep refinement and a second random seed under every predeclared gate. Timestep changes are at most 1.02% for drift and 0.38% for mean energy. The largest seed difference is 8.35% for 50 Td drift but remains within its locked uncertainty-aware allowance; all other seed differences are below 0.55%.",
  "scientific_significance": "The small timestep response makes integration discretization an unlikely explanation for the agreement with Maiorov Table 8. The field-dependent seed response independently confirms that 50 Td drift is substantially noisier and more correlated than mean energy or 100 Td drift.",
  "claim_boundary": "Two seeds establish a robustness checkpoint but do not precisely estimate the full sampling distribution. This remains one published model comparison rather than experimental or device validation.",
  "next_gate": "Acquire a traceable experimental or evaluated argon swarm reference and compare without changing the published-fit benchmark; independently extend seed count if a publication-grade 50 Td drift confidence interval is required."
